==== Buttons ====
-> [[docs:guide-user:hardware:hardware.button]] on howto use and configure the hardware button(s).

The Range Extender has two programmable buttons and a switch. The buttons are Reset,
the WiFi Protected Setup Push Button. The switch has no function, the original firmware
uses it to select whenever the wifi should operate in the 5GHz or 2.4GHz band.
Here, we merely name the buttons, so we can use them in the above Howto:

^ BUTTON   ^ Event   ^
| Reset    | reset   |
| WPS      | wps     |


===== Hardware =====

==== Serial Port ====
The UART is accessable via JP1 (which hasn't a header connected). You will need a TTL to RS232 (ie a MAX232 circuit) to utilize this. The pinout is:\\
''[GND]      [RxD] [TxD] [3.3v]''\\
''                         DJ1''

